  (:NAME "FOR-ALL" :KIND :MACRO :LAMBDA-LIST "(bindings &body body)" :DOCSTRING "Bind BINDINGS to random variables and test BODY *num-trials* times.

BINDINGS is a list of binding forms, each element is a list
of (BINDING VALUE &optional GUARD). Value, which is evaluated
once when the for-all is evaluated, must return a generator which
be called each time BODY is evaluated. BINDING is either a symbol
or a list which will be passed to destructuring-bind. GUARD is a
form which, if present, stops BODY from executing when IT returns
NIL. The GUARDS are evaluated after all the random data has been
generated and they can refer to the current value of any
binding. NB: Generator forms, unlike guard forms, can not contain
references to the bound variables.

Examples:

  (for-all ((a (gen-integer)))
    (is (integerp a)))

  (for-all ((a (gen-integer) (plusp a)))
    (is (integerp a))
    (is (plusp a)))

  (for-all ((less (gen-integer))
            (more (gen-integer) (< less more)))
    (is (<= less more)))

  (for-all (((a b) (gen-two-integers)))
    (is (integerp a))
    (is (integerp b)))" :ORIGIN "fiveam")
  (:NAME "FOR-ALL*" :KIND :MACRO :LAMBDA-LIST "(bindings &body body)" :DOCSTRING "Bind BINDINGS to random variables and test BODY *num-trials* times.

Works like FOR-ALL but variables are defined sequentially - subsequent
generator bindings may use value of a previous generator.

Example:

  (for-all* ((a (gen-integer))
             (b (gen-integer :min a :max (+ a 20)))
    (is (<= a b)))" :ORIGIN "fiveam")
  (:NAME "GEN-BUFFER" :KIND :FUNCTION :LAMBDA-LIST "(&key (length (gen-integer :min 0 :max 50)) (element-type '(unsigned-byte 8)) (elements (gen-integer :min 0 :max (1- (expt 2 8)))))" :ORIGIN "fiveam")
  (:NAME "GEN-CHARACTER" :KIND :FUNCTION :LAMBDA-LIST "(&key (code-limit char-code-limit) (code (gen-integer :min 0 :max (1- code-limit))) (alphanumericp nil))" :DOCSTRING "Returns a generator of characters.

CODE must be a generator of random integers. ALPHANUMERICP, if
non-NIL, limits the returned chars to those which pass
alphanumericp." :ORIGIN "fiveam")
  (:NAME "GEN-FLOAT" :KIND :FUNCTION :LAMBDA-LIST "(&key bound (type 'short-float))" :DOCSTRING "Returns a generator which produces floats of type TYPE. BOUND,
if specified, constrains the results to be in the range (-BOUND,
BOUND)." :ORIGIN "fiveam")
  (:NAME "GEN-INTEGER" :KIND :FUNCTION :LAMBDA-LIST "(&key (max (1+ most-positive-fixnum)) (min (1- most-negative-fixnum)))" :DOCSTRING "Returns a generator which produces random integers greater
than or equal to MIN and less than or equal to MAX." :ORIGIN "fiveam")
  (:NAME "GEN-LIST" :KIND :FUNCTION :LAMBDA-LIST "(&key (length (gen-integer :min 0 :max 10)) (elements (gen-integer :min -10 :max 10)))" :DOCSTRING "Returns a generator which produces random lists. LENGTH must be
an integer generator and ELEMENTS must be a generator which
produces objects." :ORIGIN "fiveam")
  (:NAME "GEN-ONE-ELEMENT" :KIND :FUNCTION :LAMBDA-LIST "(&rest elements)" :ORIGIN "fiveam")
  (:NAME "GEN-STRING" :KIND :FUNCTION :LAMBDA-LIST "(&key (length (gen-integer :min 0 :max 80)) (elements (gen-character)) (element-type 'character))" :DOCSTRING "Returns a generator which produces random strings. LENGTH must
be a generator which produces integers, ELEMENTS must be a
generator which produces characters of type ELEMENT-TYPE." :ORIGIN "fiveam")
  (:NAME "GEN-TREE" :KIND :FUNCTION :LAMBDA-LIST "(&key (size 20) (elements (gen-integer :min -10 :max 10)))" :DOCSTRING "Returns a generator which produces random trees. SIZE controls
the approximate size of the tree, but don't try anything above
 30, you have been warned. ELEMENTS must be a generator which
will produce the elements." :ORIGIN "fiveam")
